/**
 * AI-CONTEXT:
 *
 * Purpose:
 * - Prevents sensitive data, environment configurations, and build artifacts from being committed to version control.
 *
 * Scope:
 * - Enforces security boundaries at the git level.
 * - What it must never be responsible for: Managing actual runtime secrets.
 *
 * Critical Dependencies:
 * - Backend: None
 * - Frontend: Local development environments and CI/CD pipelines.
 * - Worker / SEO / Sitemap: None
 *
 * Security Constraints:
 * - What must never be hardcoded: Secrets, keys, IP addresses.
 * - What must remain environment-driven: All .env files MUST remain ignored.
 *
 * Non-Negotiables:
 * - .env, .env.local, .env.production, and .env.* must ALWAYS be ignored.
 * - Security violations via Git leaks are a Hard Fail.
 *
 * Change Intent:
 * - Securing the Treishvaam Agro frontend for enterprise-level Cloudflare Pages deployment.
 *
 * Future AI Guidance:
 * - Do not remove .env restrictions.
 * - If new environments are added (e.g., .env.staging), add them explicitly here.
 *
 * IMMUTABLE CHANGE HISTORY (DO NOT DELETE):
 * - ADDED:
 * • Strict .env* rules to prevent secret leakage.
 * • AI-Context block for long-term maintainability.
 * • 2026-04-09
 *
 * - EDITED:
 * • Existing node_modules and Next.js build paths retained.
 * • Why the edit was required: To ensure enterprise security standards before CI/CD pipeline integration.
 * • What behavior must remain unchanged: Build artifacts must not be tracked.
 *
 * - REMOVED:
 * • None
 *
 * - FAILED / REJECTED ATTEMPTS:
 * • None
 *
 * - DO-NOT-DELETE RULE:
 * This IMMUTABLE CHANGE HISTORY section must never be deleted,
 * truncated, rewritten, or regenerated.
 * Future AI must append only.
 */

# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.js

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# local env files (STRICTLY ENFORCED)
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local
.env.production
.env.*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts